WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.500
Good morning John

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.500
I am going to read to you my letter to 15 year old you

00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:06.740
And yes I did just hold up my bank statement acting like it was a letter

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.200
It's not, it's a bank statement.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.780
Actually it's an important update regarding

00:00:10.780 --> 00:00:12.180
my overdraft coverage.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.800
But before I read to you my important update regarding my overdraft coverage

00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:17.500
I wanted to tell you a quick story

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:20.720
Okay, last week I thought I had a super clever thought

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:25.400
I was reading Vlogbrother's comments and someone made a reference to nerds dying virgins

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.700
which is not an uncommon statement among the troll population

00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:36.060
And I just wanted to respond and say actually, I would argue that most nerds die..

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.560
And I didn't know what word to use there

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:41.100
At first I thought 'deflowered', most nerds die 'deflowered'

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:44.880
And while I think that may be technically true, depending on your perspective

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.320
It's kind of a.. the word has a negative connotation

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:53.960
Like, synonyms for 'deflowered' include like, 'corrupt' and 'sully' and 'dirtify'

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:57.200
Probably just dirty, dirty is a verb, as well as an adjective

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:00.580
And so I was thinking to myself, there is really no word for the opposite of virgin

00:01:00.580 --> 00:01:02.880
And then I thought to myself, there should be a word for that!

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:05.880
There should be a word for when there isn't a word for something

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:07.720
And I love self-referential stuff like that

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:09.200
so I thought it was super clever

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.060
so I tweeted a question to the world

00:01:11.060 --> 00:01:14.880
What's the word for when there should be a word for something but there isn't?

00:01:14.880 --> 00:01:16.800
And I did not think I was asking a serious question

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:19.080
I'd just thought I was making a funny statement

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:22.400
But then, because Nerdfighters are Nerdfighters and Nerdfighters know this stuff

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:25.260
Two very quick tweets came in from rlunny and heatherklus

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.160
informing me that there is in fact a phrase for that, not quite a word

00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:30.700
But it's called a 'lexical gap'

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:33.580
And there are a lot of lexical gaps in lots of different languages

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:36.120
for example in Romanian there's no word for shallow

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:39.560
So when you're translating into Romanian, you have to call it "not-so-deep"

00:01:39.560 --> 00:01:41.640
English also has interesting lexical gaps

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:44.240
like the fact that we have no plural for the word "you"

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:48.520
which is a big one and it results in us having to invent words like "y'all" and "youse guys"

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:51.000
and so I very excitedly @ replied both of those people.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.140
Though slightly disappointed that it was not a full word, THEN

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:58.500
Victoria tweeted saying a lexical gap or a lacuna, and I was like "a lacuna?!"

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:01.200
and so I looked up lacuna and lacuna means a lot of things

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:07.080
but if you're a linguist, a lacuna is when there is no word for something that there should be a word for

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.300
so yes there should be a word for when there should be a word for something

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.240
and there is a word for when there should be a word for something, and that word is lacuna

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:17.300
but if you're not talking to a linguist and you want to be more specific

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:19.520
you should probably use the phrase "lexical gap"

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:22.480
that is the end of my story and now I am going to read to you

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:24.300
My letter to 15-year-old John

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.000
So John, you're 15.

00:02:26.000 --> 00:02:31.540
and like most 15 year olds, you feel like when you're forced in school to do math and science and

00:02:31.540 --> 00:02:35.380
laboratory experiments, you're sort of being tortured.

00:02:35.380 --> 00:02:38.080
But here's what science does for us, 15-year-old John

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.780
it helps us understand what to think about, and it gives us a framework for how to think about those things

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:46.960
Funny this is, 15-year-old John, when you're 33, you're going to write a video letter

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.980
to 15-year-old me saying those exact same things

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:53.520
about critical reading.

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:55.280
And guess what? You'll be right!

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:58.860
Because 15 and 33-year-old John, there are lots of ways

00:02:58.860 --> 00:03:02.400
to arrive at a place where you can choose what to think about

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.980
and you know how to think about those things well

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:07.640
For you, it was reading complicated books critically

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:12.220
for me, it's statistics, and population dynamics, and evolutionary theory

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:14.860
But the truth of the matter is, to live a good life as a good person

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.540
it doesn't matter how you got there

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:18.140
It just matters that you do

00:03:18.140 --> 00:03:20.320
Also, dump your girlfriend

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:22.840
I don't know who your girlfriend is, I don't know how much like her

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:24.720
but dump her right now, because John,

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:28.360
in the future, you are going to feel much much better about yourself

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:33.180
if there is ONE girlfriend in your past that you managed to dump

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:34.540
before she dumped you

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.560
Good luck with that 15-year-old John!

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:38.920
33-year-old John, I will see you on Friday

